    "description": "Original MCQs for a personal-license exam-prep module on the North Rhine-Westphalia Fischerpruefung (fishing licence exam), covering NRW-specific closed seasons and minimum catch sizes per species (Schonzeiten/Mindestmasse, e.g. Hecht 45cm/15.Feb-30.Apr, Zander 40cm/1.Apr-31.Mai, Aal 50cm/1.Okt-1.Maerz, Lachs ganzjaehrig geschont), NRW gear and angling-method rules (verbotene Fangmittel und Elektrofischerei-Beschraenkung nach §39 LFischG, Stahlvorfach-Laengen, Pflichtausruestung, Mitfuehren von Fischereigeraet nach §49 LFischG), the NRW Fischereischein/Fischerpruefung process including the distinct Jugendfischereischein (age 10-16) and Sonderfischereischein rules (§§31-38 LFischG), general fish biology/species ID content freshly written for this module, and NRW water-protection/fisheries-oversight law (Ablassen von Gewaessern, Schonbezirke, Fischwege, Fischereiaufseher, §§41-54 LFischG). NRW has Germany's largest angler population and its own Landesfischereigesetz (LFischG NRW, Bekanntmachung der Neufassung vom 22. Juni 1994, GV. NW. S. 226/248, as amended) and Landesfischereiverordnung, distinct from the generic 'angelschein' module already in this app. Topic structure and factual grounding are drawn from the real LFischG NRW statute text (fetched directly from recht.nrw.de) and from the real topic areas and facts covered by the official NRW Fischerpruefung question catalog ('Anlage 1' to the Verwaltungsvorschrift zur Durchfuehrung des LFischG, fetched directly as a PDF from https://recht.nrw.de/system/files/BA/4679-28681-sgv_793_19971126_1_anlage1.pdf). This is a SYNTHETIC REPRODUCTION: no question, option or explanation text is copied or closely paraphrased from that official catalog at scale - every item is independently phrased from the underlying legal/factual content, citing the actual LFischG NRW paragraph in legal_basis. Schonzeit/Mindestmass figures are additionally cross-checked against two independent third-party angling-regulation summaries (schonzeiten.de and beyondfishing.de). This is a fully independent exam module - separate content pool, separate exam simulation from every other module including the generic 'angelschein' module.",
